id: pm-3os5p6
title: "pm health advises pm history-repair for history_drift_missing_stream, but history-repair refuses a stream with no entries"
description: "When an item's history stream is missing, pm health reports history_drift_missing_stream with the remedy pm history-repair <id>, rewritten to pm history-repair --all when several streams drift. history-repair cannot rebuild a missing stream: the --all row fails with 'No history entries exist for <id>; nothing to repair.' and the command exits 1. Found on PR #1762 while running the advised remedies on a mixed-drift fixture (one chain mismatch, one missing stream) in tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts. The remedy registry entry lives in src/core/diagnostics/remediation.ts, and the bulk rewrite lives in rewriteBulkHealthRemediation in src/sdk/governance/health.ts. The fix names a command that actually rebuilds or records the missing stream, for example a baseline-reseed step, or a restore when an item can be rebuilt from history; it must also keep the bulk rewrite from advising --all for a code that --all cannot repair."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: health,history,remediation,ux
created_at: "2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-21T12:39:48.889Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#27675b3cf25f0c8ca46c5936"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "An integration spec runs the remedy pm health names for a missing stream, per item and in bulk, and the history_drift check is ok afterwards"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: low
confidence: 85
expected_result: "Every remedy pm health names for history_drift_missing_stream, per item and in bulk, runs to a clean history_drift check"
actual_result: pm history-repair <id> and pm history-repair --all refuse the missing stream with 'No history entries exist; nothing to repair.' and exit 1
